│ plasma level ratios during a day were as small as 1.28 ± 0.15 in children taking a daily dose of 8 mg/kg of ZNS once │
│ a day as a single drug. The plasma level (μg/ml) to dose (mg/kg/day) ratios estimated by the trough and peak plasma  │
│ levels both increased with advancing age, but the peak‐to‐trough plasma level ratios were maintained almost          │
│ uniformly throughout the pediatric age period. A wide range of the plasma levels was associated with complete        │
