│ the controlled group. However, the clinical effects of ZNS were in agreement with the range of generally accepted    │
│ therapeutic plasma levels of ZNS, 15–40 μg/ml. Any patient who receives polytherapy is at risk to develop 1 or more  │
│ drug interactions. Concurrent administration of carbamazepine (CBZ) decreases plasma concentrations of ZNS. However, │
│ ZNS does not alter plasma concentrations of CBZ or its primary metabolite, carbamazepine‐10,11‐epoxide (CBZ‐E). It   │
